The '''Mandalore system''',<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> also known as the '''Mandalorian system''',<ref name="Corruption">{{TCW|Corruption (episode)}}</ref> was a [[star system]] located in the [[Mandalore sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]] that contained the [[planet]] [[Mandalore]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> [[homeworld]] of the [[Mandalorian]] people, its [[moon]] of [[Concordia]],<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> and the planet [[Kalevala]].<ref name="Kalevala" /> Although nominally a member of the [[Galactic Republic]], the Mandalore system declared itself neutral during the [[Clone Wars]]<ref name="Duchess of Mandalore" /> and was a member of the [[Council of Neutral Systems]] led by [[Satine Kryze]], [[duchess]] of the [[New Mandalorians]],<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> though the system itself was led by [[Prime Minister]] [[Almec]].<ref name="The Academy">{{TCW|The Academy}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Mandalore system first appeared in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in "[[The Mandalore Plot]]," the twelfth episode of the [[canon]] animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''{{'}} [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]],<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> which originally aired on [[January 29]], [[2010]].<ref name="The Mandalore Plot air date">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-mandalore-plot-episode-guide|text="The Mandalore Plot" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> It was first mentioned in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] reference book ''[[The Empire Strikes Back Sketchbook]]'', written by [[Joe Johnston]] and [[Nilo Rodis-Jamero]] and released in [[June]], [[1980]].<ref name="The Empire Strikes Back Sketchbook">''[[The Empire Strikes Back Sketchbook]]''</ref>

